From 4b4af3758863ba52ea7dcd71ddd73cf2636a7ecc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 13:24:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] target/dadao: mark jump-table destinations
 setLabelMustBeEmitted (ML-003k)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root-caused via a minimal repro (dense-range switch, 6 cases, -O0) and
llc -print-after-all: the destination MachineBasicBlock for a jump
table entry (.LBB0_1 in the repro; .LBB0_19/.LBB3_13 in the real
vfprintf.c failure) survives every single MI pass all the way through
postrapseudos — it is never removed, merged, or altered structurally.
The bug is not a codegen/pass-pipeline problem at all; it is purely in
label *emission*.

AsmPrinter::shouldEmitLabelForBasicBlock() skips printing a label for
any block with exactly one predecessor that is also its immediate
layout predecessor (isBlockOnlyReachableByFallthrough) — the ordinary,
correct behavior for a true fallthrough target, which needs no symbol.
A jump-table entry reaches its destination via an *indirect* jump
(rela+addi+BRIND), not a fallthrough, but nothing about the MI-level
CFG (a plain predecessor edge) distinguishes the two cases. At -O0,
with no block-placement pass reordering anything, DADAO's jump-table
dispatch block ends up laid out immediately before one of its own
targets often enough to hit this by coincidence — and that target's
label is silently dropped, leaving a `.quad` jump-table entry
referencing a symbol that was never printed ("Undefined temporary
symbol" at the ELF writer once MC layer bugs from ML-003e/i were
independently fixed).

The escape hatch already exists: MachineBasicBlock::
setLabelMustBeEmitted() forces the label regardless of the
fallthrough heuristic. It's normally invoked by callbr/inline-asm-goto
lowering (SelectionDAGBuilder.cpp) but ordinary switch-to-jump-table
lowering never calls it — most targets' block-placement passes at
higher opt levels keep jump-table dispatch blocks away from their own
targets, so the coincidence this needs essentially never arises there.

Fix: override AsmPrinter::emitFunctionBodyStart() to mark every
MachineBasicBlock referenced by any MachineJumpTableInfo entry before
per-block emission begins.

Verified: minimal repro (6-case dense switch) — the previously-missing
label now has exactly 1 definition, matching every other case block.
picolibc's vfprintf.c, compiled with the *exact* real build flags
(-ffunction-sections, no -fno-jump-tables, no other workaround),
compiles with 0 errors. Full end-to-end: crt0 + stdout_min.c (tinystdio
FDEV_SETUP_STREAM bridge) + printf_hello.c + a cleanly-rebuilt libc.a,
linked and run on QEMU — real output "hello, dadao" (exactly once) +
exit=0. E2E 27/27 (pre-existing suite unaffected), differential
AGREE(4-way)=200/DIVERGE=0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 llvm/lib/Target/DADAO/DADAOAsmPrinter.cpp | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Target/DADAO/DADAOAsmPrinter.cpp b/llvm/lib/Target/DADAO/DADAOAsmPrinter.cpp
index c67df53ebad9..0fa2be971d83 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/DADAO/DADAOAsmPrinter.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/DADAO/DADAOAsmPrinter.cpp
@@ -35,6 +35,31 @@ public:
     return false;
   }
 
+  // A jump-table destination block that (per the ordinary CFG predecessor
+  // analysis) has exactly one predecessor and happens to be laid out
+  // immediately after it looks, to AsmPrinter::shouldEmitLabelForBasicBlock,
+  // indistinguishable from an ordinary fallthrough target — which by design
+  // gets no label (nothing needs to name a block execution just falls into).
+  // But a jump-table entry reaches that block via an *indirect* jump
+  // (rela+addi+BRIND), not the fallthrough at all; the `.quad` entry in the
+  // table still needs a real symbol to reference. The generic mechanism for
+  // this (MachineBasicBlock::setLabelMustBeEmitted(), which forces a label
+  // regardless of the fallthrough heuristic) is normally invoked by
+  // callbr/inline-asm-goto lowering, not by ordinary switch-to-jump-table
+  // lowering — the latter has never needed it on most targets, since
+  // higher-opt-level block placement rarely lays a jump-table dispatch block
+  // directly adjacent to one of its own targets. At -O0, with no block
+  // placement pass reordering anything, DADAO hits that coincidence, and the
+  // target's label silently never gets printed — a real, verified dangling
+  // jump-table entry (`.quad .LBB0_19` with no `.LBB0_19:` anywhere in the
+  // file), confirmed via a minimal repro before this fix and gone after it.
+  void emitFunctionBodyStart() override {
+    if (const MachineJumpTableInfo *MJTI = MF->getJumpTableInfo())
+      for (const MachineJumpTableEntry &Entry : MJTI->getJumpTables())
+        for (MachineBasicBlock *MBB : Entry.MBBs)
+          MBB->setLabelMustBeEmitted();
+  }
+
   void emitInstruction(const MachineInstr *MI) override {
     if (MI->isCFIInstruction())
       return;
-- 
